ssibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible}.md | sed -n '1,240p'\nrg --files projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks | rg 'GQ0001' || true\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n### projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0001.md\n---\ntask_id: G0001\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: GB0001\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005\ntitle: Define original football question-card and catalogue bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0001\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted detailed evidence for GAME-001\u2013002/GPI-001\u2013005: card grammar, answer/explanation/provenance/accessibility fields, and four named 12-card QB-A batches with exact format/difficulty/topic quotas and two-review workflow.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md`: original question-card grammar and four named QB-A editorial batches, including permitted sources, factual and accessibility/copy reviews, provenance, version/withdrawal fields, quotas, and non-copying expression evidence.\n\nDo not author product code, implementation B/R runbooks, copied questions or reference-product expression. This task does not accept the manifest.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The finite 48-card first-release catalogue is bounded, original, and independently quota/provenance verifiable.\n### projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0002.md\n---\ntask_id: G0002\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: G0001\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,planning/game-production-inventory.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-003,GAME-004,GPI-006,GPI-007\ntitle: Define fair adjudication and editorial lifecycle bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0001\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-003\u2013004/GPI-006\u2013007: documented normalisation/alias policy, 20 fair adjudication fixtures, withdrawal states, and seeded anti-repeat/shortage policy.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md`: deterministic select/true-false/ordered/typed-answer rules, 20 fixtures, contested-fact withdrawal/provenance review states, and a seeded anti-repeat/shortage rule.\n\nNo fuzzy guessing, implementation code, B/R runbooks, or manifest acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Rules never guess answers and every catalogue-state transition is reproducible.\n### projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0003.md\n---\ntask_id: G0003\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: GB0002,G0002\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-005,GAME-006,GPI-008,GPI-009\ntitle: Define tutorial and standard-round bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0002\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-005\u2013006/GPI-008\u2013009: TUT-01\u201305, mixed 10-card round selection, optional timer, offline lifecycle, interruption and shortage behaviour.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md`: named First Whistle cards and transitions, Mixed Fixture selection/shortage fixtures, optional-off timer, offline pause/resume lifecycle, and accessibility review.\n\nDo not invent a campaign, live/ranked mode, code, B/R runbooks, or manifest acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every named tutorial card and round transition has a deterministic fixture.\n### projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md\n---\ntask_id: G0004\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: G0003\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,planning/game-production-inventory.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-007,GAME-008,GPI-010,GPI-011\ntitle: Define scoring and results bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0002\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-007\u2013008/GPI-010\u2013011: 100-point capped-streak table, feedback equivalents, result states, milestone idempotence, and 18 edge/lifecycle fixtures.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md`: score/streak rule table, 18 recovery/result fixtures, idempotent milestones, and text, non-colour, captioned/mute audio-equivalent feedback requirements.\n\nDo not create implementation code or B/R runbooks, and do not accept the manifest.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Wrong, blank, timeout, and abandon remain recoverable and do not create duplicate completion.\n### projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md\n---\ntask_id: G0005\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: GB0003,G0004\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-009,GAME-010,GAME-011,GAME-012,GPI-012,GPI-013,GPI-014,GPI-015\ntitle: Define accessible recovery and target parity bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0003\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-009\u2013012/GPI-012\u2013015: four input mappings, captions/contrast/text/motion equivalents, four recovery states, offline/update notices, and web/PWA/Android/iOS parity and certification matrix.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md`: four input mappings, accessible feedback equivalents, recovery/offline/update states, and web/PWA/Android/iOS rule/content/save parity matrix.\n\nDo not create target-exclusive content, mandatory accounts/sync, code, B/R runbooks, or manifest acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Each meaning has a non-audio, non-colour equivalent and target adaptations cannot alter shared rules or saves.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:1:# Score, streak, and results bible\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:4:`GPI-011`. This is a deterministic future-core contract, not implementation or\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:11:## GPI-010 \u2014 score and streak contract\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:20:`scoreBefore`, `streakBefore`, `scoreDelta`, `streakAfter`, and `scoreAfter`\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:21:are written to the immutable score event when the attempt resolves. The event\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:22:is the source of a reopened feedback or result surface; the score is never\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:25:| Resolved outcome | Score delta | Streak after resolution | Feedback state | Continue/recovery rule |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:27:| `correct`, streak before 0\u20131 | +100 | streak before + 1 | `correct_base` | Explanation and continue are available. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:28:| `correct`, streak before 2 | +125 | 3 | `correct_streak` | First streak bonus is +25; announce the three-in-a-row state. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:29:| `correct`, streak before 3 | +150 | 4 | `correct_streak` | Bonus rises to +50. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:30:| `correct`, streak before 4 | +175 | 5 | `correct_streak` | Bonus rises to +75. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:31:| `correct`, streak before 5 | +200 | 6 | `correct_streak_cap` | The bonus reaches its +100 cap. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:32:| `correct`, streak before 6 or more | +200 | streak before + 1 | `correct_streak_cap` | Bonus stays capped at +100; no further increase. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:38:The active streak has no maximum. After a correct resolution, `bonus =\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:39:min(100, max(0, 25 \u00d7 (streakAfter - 2)))`; thus the first three-correct streak\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:41:answer is worth at most 200 points. `scoreAfter = scoreBefore + scoreDelta`;\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:42:score is a non-negative monotonic total. `bestActiveSessionStreak` is the\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:43:maximum resolved correct streak in this run and never falls when the active\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:44:streak resets. A retry is a new `runId`; it retains aggregate history but never\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:45:overwrites the prior run's attempts or score events.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:53:| State | Required text and semantic label | Required non-colour visual | Caption/mute audio equivalent | Reduced-motion behaviour |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:55:| `correct_base` | \u201cCorrect. +100 points. Streak: N.\u201d | Success icon/pattern plus labelled score panel. | If the correct cue plays, caption `Correct; 100 points; streak N`; mute leaves all text visible. | Static labelled state; no animation required. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:56:| `correct_streak` | \u201cCorrect. +[100 + bonus] points. Streak: N. Streak bonus +[25/50/75].\u201d | Success icon/pattern plus a labelled streak marker. | Caption names correct result, points, streak, and bonus; mute changes no score information. | Replace celebration movement with static marker. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:57:| `correct_streak_cap` | \u201cCorrect. +200 points. Streak: N. Bonus capped at +100.\u201d | Success icon/pattern plus labelled cap marker. | Caption names capped bonus and points; mute changes no score information. | Static cap marker; no pulsing or forced animation. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:58:| `incorrect`, `blank`, `timeout` | Outcome name, \u201c+0 points\u201d, \u201cStreak reset\u201d, canonical answer, and explanation. | Distinct labelled error/empty/time pattern; not red or animation alone. | Caption names outcome, zero points, reset, answer, and explanation availability; mute leaves this text visible. | Static feedback and controls. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:59:| `abandoned` | \u201cRound ended. No points lost. Streak reset.\u201d plus the recovery/next action. | Distinct labelled exit/interrupted pattern. | Caption names end state and next action; mute leaves this text visible. | Static end state and focusable action. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:66:### Score and feedback edge fixtures\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:68:All fixtures start from a frozen `Mixed Fixture` run unless stated otherwise.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:74:| `SCORE-FX-01` | Correct with score 0, streak 0. | One event: `+100`, streak 1, score 100, `correct_base`; text/non-colour/caption equivalents agree. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:75:| `SCORE-FX-02` | From streak 1, correct. | One event: `+100`, streak 2, score rises by 100; no bonus message. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:76:| `SCORE-FX-03` | From score 200, streak 2, correct. | One event: `+125`, streak 3, score 325, `correct_streak`; text and caption name +25 bonus. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:77:| `SCORE-FX-04` | From score 325, streak 3, correct. | One event: `+150`, streak 4, score 475; bonus rises to +50. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:78:| `SCORE-FX-05` | From score 475, streak 4, correct. | One event: `+175`, streak 5, score 650; feedback names the +75 bonus. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:79:| `SCORE-FX-06` | From score 650, streak 5, correct; then from streak 6, correct again. | The first event is `+200`, streak 6, score 850, `correct_streak_cap`; the second is `+200`, streak 7, score 1050, proving the +100 cap does not rise. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:80:| `SCORE-FX-07` | From score 1050, streak 7, resolve `wrong`. | One zero-point event, active streak 0, score remains 1050, best streak remains 7; answer/explanation and static non-colour feedback are available. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:81:| `SCORE-FX-08` | From score 1050, streak 4, explicitly submit blank. | One zero-point `blank` event, active streak 0, score remains 1050; no answer is guessed and continue/pause remain available. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:82:| `SCORE-FX-09` | With frozen `timerMode=on`, from score 1050, streak 3, let the enabled timer expire. | One zero-point `timeout` event, active streak 0, score remains 1050; answer/explanation and static timeout feedback are available. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:83:| `SCORE-FX-10` | With frozen `timerMode=off`, wait beyond the configured duration. | No timeout, attempt, score event, or streak reset is created; card remains unresolved. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:84:| `SCORE-FX-11` | From score 450, streak 4, choose abandon; reopen the partial result. | One zero-point `abandoned` event/reset and one partial result; score remains 450, no completion milestone is awarded, and reopening returns that record. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:85:| `SCORE-FX-12` | Resolve a correct answer, then resend the same resolve command/interaction ID; enable mute and reduced motion before reopening feedback. | Exactly one attempt and score event exist; reopened feedback is static and text/non-colour equivalent remains complete with no audio required. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:87:## GPI-011 \u2014 results and local milestone contract\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:93:| `in_progress` | A run with frozen content/rules, score events, and a current safe boundary. | Resume, pause, abandon, return home only through a safe boundary. | None. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:94:| `completed_result` | Last resolved attempt is continued; immutable `ResultSummary` has `runId`, `completionId`, answered, correct, score, best active-session streak, category, outcome counts, and action labels. | Replay (new run), choose theme, exit, reopen result. | Tutorial only: request `first_whistle_complete`. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:96:| `recovery` | Draft is corrupt/incompatible or a write was interrupted; last confirmed snapshot is retained. | Resume confirmed, discard draft, return home. | None until a real completion commits. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:99:`score` and `bestActiveSessionStreak` copy the committed score-event ledger.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:101:change. It displays score, answered/correct, best active-session streak,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:108:write/retrieve the immutable `ResultSummary`, write/retrieve its aggregate\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:118:their own immutable history/result once, but cannot replace those provenance\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:124:| ID | Input / action | Expected deterministic state and idempotence result |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:126:| `RESULT-FX-01` | Complete a standard 10-card run, then reopen using its run/completion ID. | One `completed_result`, history entry, and score ledger are stored; reopen returns them without any duplicate completion or milestone. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:128:| `RESULT-FX-03` | Explicitly abandon after card 4, restart, and open its result. | One `abandoned_result`, zero-point abandon event, and no completion milestone; partial score/history is recoverable and no attempt is inferred for card 5. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:130:| `RESULT-FX-05` | On final-card completion, result write is interrupted; restart with a valid prior confirmed snapshot and corrupt draft. | Enter `recovery`, retain snapshot, offer resume-confirmed/discard-draft/return-home; no result or milestone is claimed until a successful completion commits. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:135:Release validation requires `SCORE-FX-01`\u2013`SCORE-FX-12` and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:138:score and no duplicate completion. Pause, interruption, and recovery are not\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:9:## GPI-008 \u2014 First Whistle tutorial\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:11:`First Whistle` is a fixed five-card, non-timed onboarding round. It is\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:15:published wording, answer IDs, provenance, and two reviews are governed by the\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:22:| 3 / `TUT-03` | true/false | Recognise that feedback says whether the resolved answer was accepted. | Submission resolves once; feedback is available in text plus non-colour state, then opens `TUT-04`. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:32:### Tutorial deterministic fixtures\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:39:| ID | Input / action | Expected deterministic state, record, and visible outcome |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:43:| `TUT-FX-03` | From TUT-03 submit an incorrect valid true/false value, resolve, continue. | `TUT-03 \u2192 TUT-04`; rejected text/non-colour feedback and canonical answer/explanation are recorded before continue. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:44:| `TUT-FX-04` | From TUT-04 submit its configured ordered pair, resolve, inspect explanation, continue. | `TUT-04 \u2192 TUT-05`; explanation availability is recorded; inspection does not change score, streak, or card position. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:46:| `TUT-FX-06` | Repeat the completion command in TUT-FX-05 with the same completed-run ID and interaction ID. | Return the recorded completion/result; no second milestone, history entry, or score event is added. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:50:## GPI-009 \u2014 Mixed Fixture selection\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:52:`Mixed Fixture` starts with `(catalogueSnapshotId, selectionSeed, theme,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:55:GAME-004 frozen-catalogue, publication, withdrawal, filter, anti-repeat, and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:56:SHA-256 ordering policy. It then constructs the longest deterministic prefix\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:71:### Seeded Mixed Fixture fixtures\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:93:adjudication, score, streak, or availability. Pause, background interruption,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:100:| `selecting_theme \u2192 ready` | Valid theme and deterministic selection. | Show selected count and any shortage disclosure before start. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:104:| `feedback(last) \u2192 results` | Continue after final resolution. | Commit result once; reopening is idempotent. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:107:| `paused \u2192 recovery` | Draft corrupt/incompatible or write interrupted. | Preserve last confirmed snapshot and offer resume it, discard draft, or return home; never overwrite silently. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:109:### Lifecycle deterministic fixtures\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:115:| `LIFE-FX-03` | Resolve card 1, then retry its submit command with same interaction ID. | One attempt/score event exists and active card is card 2 exactly once. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:119:| `LIFE-FX-07` | Restart with corrupt draft but valid confirmed card-4 snapshot. | Quarantine draft and offer the confirmed snapshot or discard; do not silently start a different selection. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:120:| `LIFE-FX-08` | Complete and reopen a standard result with the same completed-run ID. | Return the stored result; no duplicate aggregate history, score, or milestone is created. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:121:| `LIFE-FX-09` | From home with compatible cached package, choose the `cup` theme and leave timer off. | Traverse `home \u2192 selecting_theme \u2192 ready`; ready state shows the deterministic `MIX-FX-05` IDs/count and its reuse disclosure before start. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:123:| `LIFE-FX-11` | Resolve and continue cards 1\u20139 of LIFE-FX-01, then resolve and continue card 10. | Each of the first nine continuations traverses `feedback(card n) \u2192 active(card n+1)` after a safe save; the tenth traverses `feedback(last) \u2192 results` once. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:125:| `LIFE-FX-13` | Detect an incompatible/corrupt draft while paused and choose the recovery route. | Traverse `paused \u2192 recovery`; retain the confirmed snapshot and show resume-confirmed/discard-draft/return-home choices. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:134:motion and muted/captioned feedback. There is no ranked, daily, live, event,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:140:answer rules remain subject to the editorial/provenance validation contracts.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:12:score-event ledger, local-profile schema, confirmed-snapshot format, and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:31:reduced motion, cue volume/mute, captions/descriptions, and input help.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:41:button alone. Back never discards an unresolved answer, a draft, or local data:\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:50:announcement is the stated text once per state change; captions/descriptions\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:54:| Meaning | Required visible and semantic text | Non-colour equivalent | Audio/caption equivalent | Reduced-motion path |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:56:| Category / question context | Category name and question number (for example, \u201cWorld tournament history \u2014 Question 3 of 10\u201d). | Named category plus a distinct pattern/label; never colour alone. | No cue is required; any entry cue caption repeats the category/context. | Static panel and label; no sweep required. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:57:| Selected, unselected, and disabled answer | \u201cSelected: [answer]\u201d, \u201cNot selected\u201d, or \u201cUnavailable until [condition]\u201d. | Border, check/selection icon with accessible name, and text state. | No cue is required; any selection cue is captioned \u201cAnswer selected\u201d. | Static state change. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:58:| Correct, incorrect, blank, or enabled-timer timeout | Outcome name, points, streak result, canonical answer/explanation, and next action. | Labelled success/error/empty/time icon or pattern, not green/red alone. | Caption names the same outcome and score/streak information; mute changes no meaning. | Static feedback with no forced celebration, shake, flash, or countdown motion. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:59:| Streak / score update | \u201cScore: N. Streak: N.\u201d and, when applicable, bonus/cap text. | Labelled streak marker and numeral; not a colour, pulse, or sound alone. | Caption names points, streak, bonus, or cap. | Static score/streak marker. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:60:| Pause, saved, or recovery condition | State heading, what is retained, any risk, and named actions. | Icon/pattern is supplementary to the heading and action labels. | Caption/description repeats heading and named actions; no cue is required. | No auto-moving modal or animated warning. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:61:| Offline, update, unavailable content, or unexpected error | Plain-language notice naming availability, retained progress, and next action. | Text heading and icon/pattern; status is not conveyed through network colour alone. | If a cue plays, caption repeats the notice; mute changes no path. | Static notice; no looping spinner as the only status. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:70:`SaveSnapshot` means an immutable confirmed snapshot. A draft is never a\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:78:| `interrupted_resume` | App/browser/OS ends or backgrounds after a prior confirmed boundary. | \u201cContinue your saved round?\u201d Offer **Resume confirmed round** and **Return home**. | Restore the exact confirmed content revision, position, score ledger, and unresolved state; interruption creates no blank, timeout, abandon, or duplicate completion event. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:79:| `draft_recovery` | Draft is corrupt, incomplete, or incompatible while a confirmed snapshot exists. | \u201cA recent in-progress change could not be recovered. Your confirmed progress is safe.\u201d Offer **Resume confirmed progress**, **Discard draft**, and **Return home**. | Keep the confirmed snapshot until the player explicitly deletes local data; never silently overwrite it with the draft or a new profile. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:80:| `delete_local_data` | Player requests local-data deletion. | Confirmation names that local profile, history, results, and snapshots will be removed and cannot be resumed. Offer **Delete local data** and **Cancel**. | Only confirmed deletion clears those local records and returns to first launch. Cancel changes nothing; remote state is not implied. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:84:resolved attempt; corrupt draft with a valid snapshot; incompatible draft with a\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:101:| `CACHE-INCOMPATIBLE` | Cache cannot support the pending content version. | \u201cAn update needs a cache refresh. Your confirmed progress will be kept.\u201d | Preserve/export the confirmed snapshot before reset; provide **Refresh cache** and **Return home**. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:104:Six release fixtures are required: offline launch of First Whistle with cached\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:109:unchanged adjudication/score semantics.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:121:| Shared content, answer, score, save, recovery, result, and milestone semantics | Required; no web rule branch. | Required; no PWA rule branch. | Required; no Android rule branch. | Required; no iOS rule branch. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:123:| Accessible feedback evidence | Text scale, contrast, captions/descriptions, non-colour states, reduced motion, semantic labels. | Same shared feedback contract before/after install and offline. | Same shared feedback contract using selected OS accessibility settings. | Same shared feedback contract using selected OS accessibility settings. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:131:answer rule, score rule, save schema, or recovery guarantee for that target.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:138:  enlarged text, captions/descriptions enabled, and reduced motion enabled.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md:141:- Compare serialized confirmed snapshots and resulting score/milestone records\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:4:`GPI-007`. This is a deterministic future-core contract, not implementation or\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:54:### Twenty deterministic adjudication fixtures\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:91:transition. A revision is immutable after leaving `draft`; correction creates\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:96:| `draft` | `submit_factual_check`: provenance, originality, accepted factual review | `fact_checked` | no |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:98:| `accessibility_edited` | `accept_second_review`: distinct reviewer, grammar/alias validation | `second_reviewed` | no |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:99:| `second_reviewed` | `publish`: release editor, all release checks pass | `published` | yes |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:102:| `blocked` or `withdrawn` | `revise`: creates r+1 and preserves history/correction note | `draft` (r+1) | no |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:104:No other transition is allowed: no direct draft-to-published, self-review, or\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:106:reason/evidence, actor ID/role, and UTC time. Replay from draft reproduces\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:116:## Seeded anti-repeat and shortage policy\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:122:Draft, abandoned, and in-progress rounds do not count.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:159:alias collision, current provenance, two distinct accepted reviews, and no\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:8:## Release boundary and original-expression rule\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:31:| `id`, `revision`, `batchId`, `status` | Stable ID, positive revision, one named batch, and lifecycle: `draft \u2192 fact_checked \u2192 accessibility_edited \u2192 second_reviewed \u2192 published`; alternatively `blocked` or `withdrawn`. Only `published` is eligible. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:36:| `answerOptions` | Required only for select/true-false. Select has exactly four unique option IDs and one `correct`; true/false has canonical `true`/`false` IDs. Options are text-labelled and have non-colour selection/result states. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:40:| `provenanceId`, `factualAssertions[]` | Links each assertion to permitted durable sources/research records, source locator, checked date, and conflict/correction history. All assertions must be supported. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:41:| `reviews[]` | Two distinct completed reviews: factual/rights review and accessibility/copy review. Each carries reviewer ID/role, decision, date, findings, and revision reviewed. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:52:## Provenance and two-review workflow\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:55:`provenanceId` is `PROV-<card ID>` and must contain the precise page/document\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:57:can leave `draft`. The source family is a research route, not a substituted\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:74:assertion against the exact provenance locator, source permission and original\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:77:screen-reader text, non-colour state wording, and localisation keys. R1's\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:79:moves it to `second_reviewed`; only the release editor may then set\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:89:`status: draft`, `revision: 1`, `provenanceId: PROV-<ID>`, and two pending\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:152:| QB-A-40 | TA | 1 | Premier League all-time top scorer (as official record) \u2014 Alan Shearer | Premier League | PL |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:165:from published card records and their provenance/review records:\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:175:| Eligibility | Every card is `published`, has all grammar fields, a resolvable provenance record with a checked date, no unresolved conflict, two distinct accepted reviews of its current revision, and no withdrawal. |\n